[META]
framework: claude-framework
file_id: agent.README
class: custom
version: 1.0.0

[OVERVIEW]
purpose: Index of agent documentation for OpenGL Engine project
audience: Claude agent (compact, modular, TOON-formatted)
load_strategy: Read CLAUDE.md first, then load only files needed for current task

[PROJECT_FILES]
# Custom files — project-specific knowledge
PROJECT.toon: Project overview, modules, current status
ARCHITECTURE.toon: Layer hierarchy, module interactions, render pipeline, ECS
CONSTRAINTS.toon: 19 hard rules (memory, logging, code style, ECS, resources)
CODE_CONVENTIONS.toon: Naming, style, patterns specific to codebase
QUICK_LINKS.toon: Fast navigation to important files and concepts

[FRAMEWORK_MODULES]
# Universal files — framework-managed (do not edit, will be overwritten on patch)
learning/: Self-learning system (7 files) — when/how/where to update docs
delegation/: Subagent delegation rules (6 files) — when and how to route work
workflow/: Mandatory dev process (9 files) — DISCOVER → PLAN → CONFIRM → IMPLEMENT → VERIFY → REPORT; delivery via PR + CI (CI_PR.toon)
backlog/: Deferred-work queue (5 files + INDEX.toon) — track tasks to do later

[LOAD_ORDER]
1. CLAUDE.md (root) — critical rules and pointers
2. PROJECT.toon — what this project is
3. Task-specific:
   - Coding: ARCHITECTURE.toon + CONSTRAINTS.toon + CODE_CONVENTIONS.toon
   - Documenting: learning/ files
   - Implementing feature: workflow/ files
   - Multi-step task: delegation/ files
   - Capturing follow-up: backlog/ files
4. QUICK_LINKS.toon — when looking for specific files

[EPIC_TRACKING]
location: docs/epics/
index: docs/epics/INDEX.md
language: Russian (epic descriptions, motivation, AC)
note: Epic system pre-dates the framework's backlog/ module. Treat docs/epics/ as
      the authoritative source for large work items; backlog/ is for short-lived
      follow-ups and side-quests captured during sessions.
